      "## Advocacy begins with the client's definition of the problem",
      "Client advocacy uses professional knowledge and influence to address barriers affecting client access, rights, participation, or well-being. The counselor first asks:",
      "- What outcome does the client want?\n- How does the client understand the barrier?\n- What has already been tried?\n- What strengths, relationships, and resources are available?\n- What risks could advocacy create?\n- Does the client want coaching, accompaniment, information, a letter, coordination, or direct representation?",
