      "The ACA code directs counselors to obtain client consent before advocating on behalf of an identifiable client. A client's diagnosis, attendance, trauma history, or legal status should not be disclosed merely because it makes an argument emotionally powerful.",
      "Before contacting a school, employer, insurer, housing program, court-related entity, or service agency:",
      "- Verify the client's authorization and decision-making authority.\n- Clarify recipient, purpose, scope, and expiration.\n- Share only what supports the requested goal.\n- Explain foreseeable benefits and risks.\n- Use a secure channel.\n- Document the request, consent, action, and result.",
