      "“The client needs to advocate for themselves” can become a justification for withholding needed support. Consider whether the client:",
      "- Understands the system and language\n- Has access to records, technology, transportation, or communication aids\n- Faces retaliation or discrimination\n- Has sufficient time, energy, or safety\n- Can use coaching, rehearsal, or supported communication\n- Wants the counselor present",
